      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking at some weird latency on a subnet here in Lyon. Getting intermittent packet loss and jitter on the 10.24.15.0/24 range. Here's a traceroute snippet from one of the affected nodes:\n\n1  192.168.1.1  0.523 ms  0.489 ms  0.512 ms\n2  10.0.0.1  12.451 ms  45.892 ms  15.231 ms\n3  172.16.45.2  112.03 ms  158.42 ms  134.11 ms\n4  82.12.4.102  145.22 ms  312.90 ms  148.55 ms\n5  82.12.4.103  146.10 ms  298.12 ms  147.90 ms\n\nThe jitter seems to spike heavily at hop 3 and 4. Can you help me figure out if this looks like a routing loop, a saturated link, or maybe something physical with the cabling?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
